@manauref
manauref
2 days ago
Collaborator
seems to me there are a couple of reasons the code can get status = false here, and then return 0 in line 263.

But if you look at gyrokinetic/zero/gk_geometry_mirror.c lines 61-127, the
struct gkyl_mirror_grid_gen * objects are created and never checked whether they are nonzero or non-NULL, so the code proceeds even though these objects were not created.

I think there should be an assert, either in this file or in gyrokinetic/zero/gk_geometry_mirror.c to avoid this.

