{"body":"I don't think the changes in this file are warranted. I've produced exact particle and energy balance on multiple GPUs (see nonuniform v paper).","path":"gyrokinetic/apps/gk_species_bflux.c"}
{"body":"These changes are necessary in 1x (not in 2x or 3x). Comm_plane[0] is the full communicator, so otherwise the reduction includes fluxes at internal rank boundaries. In 2D/3D, the plane communicators already isolate the boundary slabs, which is consistent with your successful multi-GPU balances.","path":"gyrokinetic/apps/gk_species_bflux.c"}
{"body":"Can you provide more details about the `# Bugs were fixed in the geometry modules` ?\nWe would need to know what's changed in other than mirror setup too. As we discussed the other time, I think it's worth creating a pdf with plot comparison for all these diff reg tests between main and this branch as done in, e.g., https://github.com/gkeyllorg/gkeyll/pull/1175","path":"ci/jenkins/expected_regression_diffs.txt"}
{"body":"This is saying that these regression tests use geometry which was changed in this pull request. Since the geometry changed, the results will changed. There are some changes in mapc2p and tokamak geometries as well, which is why it's not just mirror ones being skipped.","path":"ci/jenkins/expected_regression_diffs.txt"}
{"body":"seems to me there are a couple of reasons the code can get `status = false` here, and then return 0 in line 263.\n\nBut if you look at gyrokinetic/zero/gk_geometry_mirror.c lines 61-127, the\n`struct gkyl_mirror_grid_gen *` objects are created and never checked whether they are nonzero or non-NULL, so the code proceeds even though these objects were not created.\n\nI think there should be an assert, either in this file or in gyrokinetic/zero/gk_geometry_mirror.c to avoid this.","path":"gyrokinetic/zero/mirror_grid_gen.c"}
